  "name": "Question 14",
  "problem": "What linear transformation is represented by the following matrix\n$[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]?$",
  "worked_solution": "We can find the images of the standard basis vectors $i$ and $j$ under the action of  $T,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(i) & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=i \\\\ T(j) & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=4i+j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix represents a *horizontal* shear with a shear factor of $4.$",
